      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-08-show-hn-chiptune-radio",
      "title": "Show HN: Chiptune Radio",
      "summary": "I built a chiptune song generator and its broadcasting algorithmically generated chiptune music.\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48826094\nPoints: 45\n# Comments: 9",
      "body": "Chiptune Radio is a side project of Aleph Void, LLC — the music of sound chips past, streaming while you work, reverse engineer, or just vibe.\nMusic composed for and inspired by classic sound hardware — the SID, the NES APU, the Game Boy's four channels, and the tracker scene that keeps them alive.\nA continuous radio-style broadcast on Twitch. Drop in any time, leave it on in the background, and let the playlist do the work.\nBuilt and operated by Aleph Void, LLC — a software security and reverse engineering firm with a soft spot for old hardware and the sounds it makes.",
