      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-07-google-s-pixel-event-is-set-for-august-12",
      "title": "Google’s Pixel event is set for August 12",
      "summary": "Google's upcoming event in August will introduce new Pixel devices.",
      "body": "11:38 AM PDT · July 7, 2026\nGoogle is preparing for its Made by Google launch event, which is scheduled for August 12 in New York City, as announced on Tuesday.\nWe’re hoping this event will be less cringeworthy than last year’s, which featured Jimmy Fallon and other celebrities, including Stephen Curry and the Jonas Brothers.\nGoogle Pixel event – August 12 pic.twitter.com/Veo1RCJN7j— Mark Gurman (@markgurman) July 7, 2026\nOther leaks suggest that the base Pixel 11 may come with slimmer bezels and a sleek black camera bar, while the Pixel 11 Pro is rumored to be slightly thinner than its predecessor. Additionally, there is speculation about the Pixel 11 Pro Fold, which might have a redesigned camera bump and a lighter profile compared to the previous model.\nOn a negative note, one report suggests that Google may skip the 128GB option for the new models, starting instead with 256GB, which could lead to a higher price tag.\nLast year, the event took place on August 20, where Google announced the Pixel 10 series, AI-powered upgrades, and other devices, including a new foldable, the Pixel Watch 4, and the second generation of its budget-friendly A-Series earbuds.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Lauren Forristal",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-07T18:38:29.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Google-Pixel-10.png?w=1200",
